# Typography

Three roles. Pick by **authorship**, not taste.

| Role | Token / component | Use for |
|---|---|---|
| Display | `<Heading level="display-lg\|md\|sm">` or `type.display*` | Page title, diagnostic step name, brand moment. **Max 1–2 per screen.** Never body copy, buttons, or repeating card titles. |
| Body | `<Text variant="body-lg\|md\|sm\|caption">` or `type.body*` / `type.caption` | Questions, descriptions, names, UI labels, section titles. Default for everything a person wrote. |
| Mono | `<Mono variant="label\|sm\|md">` or `type.mono*` | Ids, dates, statuses, codes, admin column headers. Machine/system content only. |

- Do not set `font-size`, `line-height`, or `letter-spacing` inline or as `text-[Npx]`. Add a named token in `src/styles/tailwind.css` `@theme` if a new size is needed.
- Enforced by `local/no-arbitrary-text-size` (`npm run lint`) and `npm run lint:typography`.
- Do not use `font-display` outside `Heading`, `AuthLayout` wordmark, or `AdminLayout` wordmark.
- One scale for all ages. Age differences live in copy, not type size/weight.
- Exceptions (do not "fix"): Spine step numerals, OTP cell digits, emoji/icon sizes, Likert pole-label clamp. See `src/shared/ui/typography/tokens.ts`.
